# decibel_TENOR_2026 is PUBLIC. Nothing personal lands here: no call screenshots, no account details, no licensed fonts.
# Carried from piece #6 `septet_LGMF_2026/.gitignore` @ 2e5ac56 (the new-piece protocol's 2.4). The paths below are the
# stack's; they take effect when the code arrives with the copy-forward (container 3).

# Node
node_modules/

# Reaper — the rack (.rpp) IS committed; these are not
*.rpp-bak
*.reapeaks
reaper/media/
reaper/Media/
reaper/Backups/
reaper/AutoSaves/

# Composer score — canonical scores/*.json ARE committed; safety-net versions and the
# autosave working copies are not (piece #3 D8, piece #4 D10)
scores/versions/
scores/*-work.json

# Fonts are licensed software and this repo is public (piece #4, day 36) — never committed.
# Root only: notation/app/fonts/ holds Crimson Pro, which is under the SIL Open Font
# Licence (Google Fonts) and may be redistributed; the app, export_print and export_video
# read it from there.
/fonts/

# Derivable render outputs
notation/video/**/*.mp4
notation/video/**/*.png
notation/video/**/*.rgba
notation/video/test/
notation/video/probe/
notation/video/renders/demos/
print/score/*.pdf
print/score/*.__print.html
# PLAN 2b.6: the APPROVED copy too — a print PDF lives on this machine only, as the
# approved video does (notation/video/**/*.mp4). Its archive README is what git carries.
print/score/**/*.pdf

# the call's screenshots (his, 2026-10-03: "A, keep it local") — this repo is public and they show his account's address
docs/call/

# Probe / research artefacts
probes/_selftest_render.wav
probes/last_bend_analysis.json
research/audio/*.wav
research/audio/*.flac

# THE ELECTRONICS' BANK (PLAN 1.1 · 6.3b): the whole recordings stay on this machine, kept for a re-crop;
# the cropped samples (bank/samples/*.wav) and the index WERE committed — the samples are the piece's (DEC-1) — UNTIL 2026-10-06:
# THE COMPOSING BANK IS NOT COMMITTED (his word, journal D18 · RUNNING_LOG §193: "keep a bank of samples just uncommitted here
# in the repo"): every sample under bank/samples/ stays on his disk from here on — the batch of DEC-37 and whatever he captures
# while composing; the index IS committed (the record of what the bank held). The 60 that were tracked are untracked too
# (RUNNING_LOG §196: his passes re-capture them — on his disk still, in the history still; `git add -f` brings one back).
# The concert's bank is the recording session's, a decision of its own then.
bank/samples/*.wav
bank/samples/raw/
# THE PLAN'S RENDERS are NOT committed (his word "b", 2026-10-05, journal D16 · RUNNING_LOG §149): a variant of the processed return,
# <sample>~<key>-<env>.wav, is re-made from bank/presets.json at every pass and every "render all planned" — an evening of
# throws made 632 of them, 95 MB. They stay on his disk. A workshop stage, <root>~<n>.wav (no hyphen after the ~), IS committed.
bank/samples/*~*-*.wav

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# the Reaper bridge runtime (PLAN 0k) and Kontakt proof outputs
reaper/bridge/inbox/
reaper/bridge/outbox/
reaper/bridge/done/
reaper/bridge/heartbeat.json
reaper/kontakt/out/
probes/__pycache__/

# RUNNING_LOG §453 (2026-09-13): the Reaper renders (~190 MB each) and the raw capture of the composer's playback stay out of git;
# the MIDI files they come from are committed.
notation/audio/*.wav
notation/audio/raw/
midi/*.capture.json

midi/*/*.evt
reaper/*_render.rpp
reaper/*_render.rpp-bak

# the calibration reference (PLAN 1b.1) — generated byte-identical from a seed by
# tools/make_reference_audio.js; its SHA-256 is recorded in bank/reference.json
probes/reference/*.wav

# THE ELECTRONICS' BANKS (RUNNING_LOG §71): the backup bank's raw windows and the concert's live captures stay on this machine;
# bank/backup/*.wav and its index ARE committed, like bank/samples (the players' recordings are the piece's)
bank/backup/raw/
bank/live/
# the crop test's page and sounds (node tools/elec.js croptest) — regenerated at will
score/public/crop_test/
